WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Every routine change
arrives as a typed request.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:08.388
The help desk catalog has ten items, for
joiners, movers, leavers, credentials,

3
00:00:08.388 --> 00:00:12.595
groups, licenses, Conditional
Access exceptions and guests,

4
00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:17.812
each bound to the control it exercises
and the approval that control needs.

5
00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:22.000
Each item closes only when a read
of the target confirms the change.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.620
The leaver fails audits most often:
disable the account, revoke sessions,

7
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.625
deprovision every connected application,
and reassign what the person owned.

8
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:35.596
And federal 911 rules bind
whoever operates the phone system,

9
00:00:35.596 --> 00:00:39.800
so a validated emergency address
gates every number assignment.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.400
SaaS integration is the densest moment.

11
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.173
In GCC, an administrator sees the full
commercial application gallery and can

12
00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:50.625
federate a third-party service
in about fifteen minutes,

13
00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:54.150
and nothing in the vendor's
path asks about authorization.

14
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.869
Restricting consent
decides who may approve,

15
00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:59.588
not whether the service
may hold federal data.

16
00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:05.112
So the catalog records a FedRAMP Marketplace
verdict before anything is configured,

17
00:01:05.112 --> 00:01:09.290
with Class C or higher as the
program's default for identity data.
